      "question": "What is the output of the following code snippet?\n#include <stdio.h>\nint main() {\n    int a[] = {1, 2, 3, 4};\n    int sum = 0;\n    for(int i = 0; i < 4; i++) {\n        sum += a[i];\n    }\n    printf(\"%d\", sum);\n    return 0;\n}",
      "options": {
        "A": "1",
        "B": "4",
        "C": "20",
        "D": "10"
      },
      "correct": "D",
      "explanation": "The loop adds every element of {1, 2, 3, 4}, giving 1 + 2 + 3 + 4 = 10. Option 20 would require each value to be counted twice.",
      "topicQuality": "specific"
    },
